  "description": "High-performance, spec-compliant ULIDs engineered to prevent index fragmentation and random-part overflow errors.\n\nIdeal for database primary keys and distributed systems, this library ensures lexicographical sortability and human-readable Base32 encoding. It features configurable protection against enumeration attacks, is fully Native AOT-ready, and offers zero-allocation interoperability with GUIDs, databases, and JSON. Optimized for efficient database writes and robust, timestamped identification in modern .NET.",
